		{
			"id": "link-61dbbaec71b9f7ece8a881b2da57409e",
			"title": "Dolly Parton's Imagination Library",
			"link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474",
			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474\"><span>Dolly Parton's Imagination Library</span></a><a href=\"https://imaginationlibrary.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"Story_link\">(https://imaginationlibrary.com/)</a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474\">682 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=jumploops\"><span>jumploops</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474\">3 days ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474\">111 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>With today's news, I thought I'd share this great program:<p>“When I was growing up in the hills of East Tennessee, I knew my dreams would come true. I know there are children in your community with their own dreams. They dream of becoming a doctor or an inventor or a minister. Who knows, maybe there is a little girl whose dream is to be a writer and singer.</p><p>The seeds of these dreams are often found in books and the seeds you help plant in your community can grow across the world.”</p></span></div></div></div></div>",
			"retrieved": 1793049082344
		},
		{
			"id": "link-d2d147873d73c857a64872018464431a",
			"title": "Ask HN: If the models are so good, why doesn't OpenAI just start 100 companies?",
			"link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997",
			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997\"><span>Ask HN: If the models are so good, why doesn't OpenAI just start 100 companies?</span></a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997\">679 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=ex-aws-dude\"><span>ex-aws-dude</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997\">6 days ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997\">752 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>Title is a bit of an exaggeration but the question is more: if the frontier models are so good, why even sell them as your primary money maker?<p>Couldn't OpenAI or Anthropic make a lot more money by just starting companies themselves that leverage the models and building their own products?</p><p>Is selling tokens really the best strategy?</p><p>Especially with commodification and prices declining wouldn't that indicate there is more money to be made on the application-side of the models rather than the utility side</p></span></div></div></div></div>",
			"retrieved": 1792858451928
		},
